  "structural_review": {
    "classes_per_jar": 31,
    "declared_methods_and_constructors_per_jar": 105,
    "verification": "Existing JDK21 java -Xverify:all, Class.forName(name,false,isolated-loader), declared methods/constructors/fields resolved. No wrapper initialization or method invocation. Full static javap disassembly retained locally.",
    "native_methods": 0,
    "invokedynamic_sites": 0,
    "cross_version_comparison": "30 of 31 classfiles are byte-identical. Install.class changes only the checksum-error diagnostic string; its disassembled instructions and method/field targets are unchanged."
  },
  "security_review": [
    "Reviewed entry/argument/configuration flow, all external method/field targets and the network, credential, process, reflection, checksum and extraction paths against the complete disassembly. CLI helpers use string/collection/regex state and errors; there is no native or dynamic-bootstrap method.",
    "Download reads only its supplied Gradle distribution URI. Basic authentication uses explicitly configured Gradle wrapper credentials or URI userinfo; proxy authentication is restricted to PROXY requests and configured protocol proxy properties. This is an intentional credential capability, not permission to execute the wrapper or transmit secrets.",
    "The only environment lookup is GRADLE_USER_HOME. Properties input files are the configured Gradle user/project properties; only systemProp-prefixed entries become JVM properties. No browser, keychain, SSH, cloud-token or wallet access was found.",
    "The sole ProcessBuilder call is the fixed three-argument chmod 755 <canonical Gradle executable path>, with no shell. Classloader/reflection targets are the Gradle launcher main method and Java Base64 compatibility helpers; wrapper code does not fetch or evaluate arbitrary inline script.",
    "ZIP extraction passes every entry name through PathTraversalChecker.safePathName. SHA256 verification compares the completed distribution file, deletes the mismatching cached distribution and throws. The wrapper allows a missing distribution checksum by design: this review does not clear missing checksums or distribution/Gradle graph verification.",
    "All existing constant-string malware inspection and native/unknown coverage rules remain active. Exact whole-JAR bytes and containing member path must match before any of these classfiles can be recognized. Changed ZIP metadata, payload, member paths or classes require a new review."
  ],
